WEBVTT

00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:21,240
What else, besides the glutathione, will keep the cancer cells alive at a good shape that we should stay away from?

00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:27,240
Well, you should stay away from antioxidants if you have cancer.

00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:31,240
Now, there's argument that, okay, my cancer is not active.

00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:35,240
I've been full remission. I've been in full remission now for three years.

00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:38,240
Should I start taking antioxidants?

00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:43,240
Well, you could argue that. You know that, okay, well, you're in full remission.

00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:48,240
No, let's try to make sure you don't get cancer elsewhere.

00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:56,240
So, I'm not against, it's just because a person has had cancer at one point in time doesn't mean they could never take antioxidants again.

00:00:56,240 --> 00:01:10,240
No, but when you have active cancer and it is active and you don't have it in full remission, or you just maybe are calling it a ton and everything to go on antioxidants is not a good idea.

00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:28,240
So, it would be any antioxidants glutathione is just the primary and most active intracellular antioxidant.

00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:38,240
So, no, there's some nutrients that act like antioxidants that can be good for certain cancers though.

00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:54,240
So, it's not just a clear cut thing, but it's like lung cancer is a little bit different where certain things that act as antioxidants elsewhere actually help with lung cancer.

00:01:54,240 --> 00:02:01,240
So, it's not perfectly clear cut. Glutathione though, that's just across the board, no matter what cancer.

00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:07,240
Because that is the primary intracellular antioxidant.

00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:18,240
So, again, like that person who said my IV therapist wants to put me an IV glutathione, it just does not make any sense whatsoever to me.

00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:23,240
I don't know why, they're not looking at the data there.

